# PinoyBusinessPOS React Card Standard

For PinoyBusinessPOS React card / container presentation work:

1. Follow `src/Products/PinoyBusinessPOS/Docs/UI/exits-card-standard.md` (authoritative contract).
2. Reuse `components/ui/card.tsx` + `components/exits/card-variants.ts`. Do **not** invent page-local visual Card systems when the shared foundation can express the need.
3. Keep **type/purpose**, **treatment**, and **motion** independent. Locked types: BASIC · SUMMARY · KPI · ACTION · ENTITY · PRODUCT · SELECTABLE · STATUS · COMPACT · FEATURED. Treatments: SURFACE · BORDERED · ELEVATED · INTERACTIVE · SELECTED · ACCENT · FEATURED. Layouts: VERTICAL · HORIZONTAL. Motion: STATIC · LIFT · EXPAND · ACCENT · MEDIA ZOOM · HOVER REVEAL.
4. Defaults: information → BORDERED/SURFACE + STATIC; clickable entity → LIFT; prominent clickable → EXPAND (`expandScale` standard ≈ 1.02, transform only); selectable → selection feedback (no strong expand); KPI → STATIC unless clickable; featured → Featured/Accent + EXPAND.
5. Style selected / accent / featured through ExItS Primary tokens — **PRIMARY is not hardcoded green**. SUCCESS/WARNING/DANGER/INFO accents stay semantic.
6. Reuse locked Button, Chip, Tabs, and ExitsTable inside Cards — do not invent Card-local button/chip/tab/table styling.
7. Preserve Preferences theme (light / dark / system) and density (compact / balance / comfort). Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Prefer logical properties for RTL accents and indicators.
8. Static Cards must not imitate interactive Cards. Hover must not hide required business functionality. Selectable ≠ Interactive.
9. Not everything needs a Card — avoid nested Cards and decorative boxes with no grouping purpose.
10. Explicit task overrides take precedence over standard defaults. Domain correctness and accessibility remain mandatory.

Keep detailed rules in the markdown standard. Visual reference: `/ui-standards` → Cards.
Do not modify the locked Table, Button, Chip, or Tabs standards.
